<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
     Local manifest for malbec (Lenovo TB390FU) on LineageOS 23.2.

     Copy to .repo/local_manifests/malbec.xml in a fresh checkout, then
     `repo sync`.

     ⚠️ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS INSTEAD OF `breakfast malbec`

     `lineage.dependencies` is the LineageOS-native mechanism and it CANNOT work
     for a personal fork. vendor/lineage/build/tools/roomservice.py hardcodes the
     LineageOS organisation in two places:

         line 222   'name': f'LineageOS/{repo_name}'
         line 327   git ls-remote https://:@github.com/LineageOS/<repo_name>

     and the `remote` escape at lines 226 to 233 applies only to `aosp-*`
     remotes; for anything else it sets project.remote and leaves the
     LineageOS-prefixed name in place. So a dependency written as

         "repository": "suddenBook/proprietary_vendor_lenovo_malbec"

     is probed as `LineageOS/suddenBook/proprietary_vendor_lenovo_malbec`, comes
     back with no branches, and roomservice.py line 349 exits with

         Default revision lineage-23.2 not found in ... Bailing.

     Moving the three repos onto the `lineage-23.2` branch was a real and
     separate bug, and fixing it was necessary but not sufficient: the
     organisation prefix cannot be fixed from the device tree at all. Hence this
     file.

     `lineage.dependencies` is kept as it is. It is correct, and it starts
     working the day these repos live under LineageOS.

     ⚠️ AFTER SYNCING, BEFORE BUILDING

     One blob (libarcsoft_faceid.so, 134 MB) is above GitHub's per-file limit and
     is stored with Git LFS. Run the two LFS commands in the device tree's
     README before the first build. Skipping them leaves a 134-byte text file in
     place of the library and the build stops with "must have a valid ELF magic
     word", which reads like a corrupt blob rather than a missing object.
-->
<manifest>
  <remote name="suddenBook"
          fetch="https://github.com/suddenBook"
          revision="refs/heads/lineage-23.2" />

  <project path="device/lenovo/malbec"
           name="android_device_lenovo_malbec"
           remote="suddenBook" />

  <project path="device/lenovo/malbec-kernel"
           name="android_device_lenovo_malbec-kernel"
           remote="suddenBook" />

  <project path="vendor/lenovo/malbec"
           name="proprietary_vendor_lenovo_malbec"
           remote="suddenBook" />
</manifest>
